==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|s|u}}

===Etymology===
Agent participle of ''*sure-'' "to die" (see  {{term|lang=fi|surra}}). Cognate with Estonian {{term|lang=et|surm}}.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[violent]] [[death]], mainly used of humans.
#* ''He saivat surmansa'' = They got killed (literally: “they got their deaths”).
# [[personification|Personification]] of sudden [[death]].
#* ''Hän joutui '''surman''' suuhun'' = He got killed (literally: "he got into the mouth of death'").
# {{context|legal|lang=fi}} [[killing|Killing]], [[voluntary]] [[manslaughter]] under [[mitigating]] circumstances.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-koira|surm|||a}}

====Usage notes====
* (''law'') ''Killing'' is the ''unofficial'' translation of Finnish penal code used by the Ministry of Justice of Finland. See usage notes under {{term|tappo}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|voluntary manslaughter}}  [[tappo]] {{qualifier|common language}}

